<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Taking Care of Our Class – Lesson # 1</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Taking Care of Our Class</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> We Are Sweeping the Floors.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Identify specific information in announcements or recordings. Interactive: Ask for repetition and clarification in a conversation about known topics.</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can identify specific information in announcements about classroom tasks (e.g., "Team One sweeps the floor, and Team Two arranges the desks."). Can ask for repetition and clarification in conversations about classroom tasks (e.g., "Can you repeat which team cleans the board?" "Can you say that again? Who arranges the desks?"). Can identify specific details in recordings about classroom cleaning activities (e.g., "We sweep the floor.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. Activating prior knowledge and introducing core vocabulary for the theme "We Are Sweeping the Floors."</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays flashcards or realia of classroom objects and cleaning supplies (e.g., chair, desk, trash can, broom, dustpan, mop, sponge, bucket, cloth, cleaner). Students listen and point to the correct item as the teacher names them. Teacher asks, "What do we see?" "What is this?" to elicit simple responses or pointing. For example, "This is a chair. What is this?" (pointing to a broom).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words: /r/ in "arrange" and /s/ in "supply." Teacher says words like "sweep," "wipe," "arrange," "tidy," "clean up" while performing exaggerated actions. Teacher says, "We are sweeping the floor." (demonstrating) and "Please arrange the chairs." Teacher also models the compound word "whiteboard," breaking it into syllables: "white-board, two syllables."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the new vocabulary and actions.
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Holding a mop) "Is this a broom or a mop?" (Expected answer: "A mop.")</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Mimicking sweeping) "Am I sweeping or wiping?" (Expected answer: "Sweeping.")</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Pointing to arranged chairs) "Are the chairs messy or tidy?" (Expected answer: "Tidy.")</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class." Introducing context through an authentic listening text.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An audio recording of a short classroom announcement about daily cleaning tasks. The recording features clear, slow speech suitable for A1.3 learners, focusing on imperatives, present continuous, and "can." (e.g., "Good morning, class! It's cleaning time. Team One, please sweep the floor and arrange the chairs. Team Two, you are wiping the desks. You can clean the whiteboard too. Remember to put away the cleaning supplies carefully. Let's make our classroom clean and tidy!").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Receptive: Identify specific information in announcements or recordings.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question (1st Listening):</b> "What is the announcement about?" (Expected: "Cleaning the classroom.")</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Specific Information (2nd Listening - True/False):</b> Students listen and mark T/F for statements like: "Team One is wiping the desks." (F) "Team Two cleans the whiteboard." (T - or inferred, "can clean"). "They are putting away supplies." (T)</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching (3rd Listening - Information Matching):</b> Students listen and match "Team One" or "Team Two" to their tasks (e.g., "sweep the floor," "arrange the chairs," "wipe the desks," "clean the whiteboard").</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening. Practicing identifying specific language structures and vocabulary in controlled and semi-controlled listening activities.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice listening for present continuous ("We are sweeping."), imperatives ("Sweep the floor."), and modal "can" ("Can you help me wipe?"). Target vocabulary includes nouns (chair, desk, mop, sponge), verbs (sweep, wipe, arrange, clean up), and adjectives (tidy, clean).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Listening & Selection:</b> The teacher plays short audio clips of sentences related to classroom cleaning. Students have a worksheet with two picture options for each sentence. They listen and circle the picture that matches the audio. For example, Audio: "We are sweeping the floor." Students circle the picture of someone sweeping vs. someone wiping. Audio: "Please arrange the chairs." Circle picture of chairs being arranged vs. chairs being messy.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Listening & Gap-fill:</b> The teacher plays audio sentences with a missing word. Students listen and fill in the blank on their worksheet using a word bank (e.g., sweep, wipe, arrange, can, please). Audio: "Team One, ______ the floor." (sweep). Audio: "______ you help me clean the board?" (Can). Audio: "Let's clean up the desks, ______." (please). This activity also reinforces sociolinguistic use of "please."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Listening & Clarification Drill:</b> Students work in pairs. Partner A describes a simple classroom task using an imperative or "can" (e.g., "Sweep the area around the trash can." "Can you tidy the books?"). Partner B listens and repeats the task to confirm, or asks for repetition/clarification using target phrases: "Can you repeat, please?" or "Say that again? Who is sweeping?" This directly addresses the interactive listening objective.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class." Focusing on fluency and collaborative interaction.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: "Classroom Cleaning Crew - Listening Challenge"</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students are divided into small "cleaning crews" (3-4 students). The teacher plays a pre-recorded audio of the "Principal's Announcement" giving specific, multi-step instructions for classroom cleaning. Each crew needs to listen carefully to identify their assigned tasks and the cleaning supplies they need. The instructions will include present continuous, imperatives, and "can." (e.g., "Hello, Cleaning Crew A! You are sweeping the floor very carefully, and then you can put away the chairs. Cleaning Crew B, please wipe the desks quickly and arrange the tables. Don't forget the cleaning supplies: dustpan, mop, cloth, cleaner!").</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After listening, each crew discusses and decides their tasks. One student from each crew then reports back to the teacher, stating their tasks (e.g., "We are sweeping the floor and putting away the chairs.") and confirming they understood, or asking for clarification if they missed a detail (e.g., "Can you say that again? Which team is cleaning the whiteboard?"). This promotes collaborative listening and sociolinguistic interaction with "please."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluent identification of specific information from an announcement and confident use of phrases for repetition and clarification in a group interaction.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of listening comprehension and ability to ask for clarification. Encouraging student self-assessment.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the "Classroom Cleaning Crew" activity and a short listening quiz. The checklist focuses on students' ability to identify tasks and use clarification phrases.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher plays a final, short audio recording of three instructions for cleaning the classroom (e.g., "Team Yellow is organizing the books. Team Green is wiping the windows. Team Blue, please sweep quietly."). Students listen and write down the task for each team on a simple worksheet. Additionally, the teacher asks one student a direct question based on the audio, and observes if the student can answer or ask for repetition/clarification if needed.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurately identifies at least 2 out of 3 specific tasks from the audio recording.</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Attempts to ask for repetition or clarification at least once during interaction or in response to a direct question, using phrases like "Can you repeat, please?" or "Say that again?".</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrates understanding of target vocabulary and grammar (present continuous, imperatives).</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can identify (2 or 3) cleaning tasks in an announcement." (Students circle a number).</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I asked for repetition or clarification today: Yes / No."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I learned today is: __________."</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Reflecting on the learning process and planning for future lessons within the theme sequence.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of listening to the cleaning instructions was most challenging for me today?"</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I can do to improve my listening skills next time?"</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
          <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., Students were engaged with the visual aids and TPR, the clarity of the audio recordings was appropriate for A1.3, students actively tried to use clarification phrases in pairs.)</p>
          <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Some students struggled with differentiating between "sweep" and "mop"; I need to reinforce the pronunciation of "supply" more. Perhaps add an extra visual cue for each cleaning verb.)</p>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Great job listening today, everyone! Next time, we will *read* some short texts about how different cleaning teams take care of their classrooms, using many of the same words we learned today."</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>